00:46:53.370 --> 00:46:55.860
- If I turn to RSP,

00:46:55.860 --> 00:46:57.360
which I haven't mentioned this paper,

00:46:57.360 --> 00:46:59.490
but is obviously an important
part of intervention

00:46:59.490 --> 00:47:01.143
in the most challenged systems.

00:47:02.340 --> 00:47:05.160
When a system is at NOF four,

00:47:05.160 --> 00:47:07.500
it is allocated an improvement director

00:47:07.500 --> 00:47:09.210
and that improvement
director is responsible

00:47:09.210 --> 00:47:11.160
for making a plan with the trust

00:47:11.160 --> 00:47:13.320
or the system about what
are all of the levers

00:47:13.320 --> 00:47:16.380
that need to be pulled in
order for that trust to exit

00:47:16.380 --> 00:47:21.065
from NOF four and dropped NOF
three or improved NOF three.

00:47:21.065 --> 00:47:24.940
And as the system is been going for

00:47:25.860 --> 00:47:27.960
I think 2 1/2 years formally,

00:47:27.960 --> 00:47:30.870
we now know we have
better data effectively

00:47:30.870 --> 00:47:33.960
on what have been the most
effective interventions.

00:47:33.960 --> 00:47:36.510
We do have a systems have a successful

00:47:36.510 --> 00:47:37.674
record of leaving NOF

00:47:37.674 --> 00:47:41.340
and improving their
performance substantively.

00:47:41.340 --> 00:47:43.800
And we have systems that
have been in NOF four,

00:47:43.800 --> 00:47:46.233
for almost the entire
time that it's existed.

00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:49.200
So one of the things
we're doing in concert

00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:52.140
with looking at the
overall operating model

00:47:52.140 --> 00:47:53.910
is what are the actually effective

00:47:53.910 --> 00:47:56.010
improvement interventions,

00:47:56.010 --> 00:47:58.260
whether that's in finance, in leadership,

00:47:58.260 --> 00:48:01.500
in operational performance,
in clinical quality management

00:48:01.500 --> 00:48:04.481
and trying to get better
codified at those.

00:48:04.481 --> 00:48:06.900
But what we have to sign off

00:48:06.900 --> 00:48:11.850
at the beginning of each RSP discussion

00:48:11.850 --> 00:48:13.890
is exactly how long do we think this trust

00:48:13.890 --> 00:48:15.450
should be in NOF four?

00:48:15.450 --> 00:48:17.520
And then measuring progress against that

00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:19.860
and the quality committee reviews

00:48:19.860 --> 00:48:21.750
that on a regular basis.

00:48:21.750 --> 00:48:23.010
In terms of finite resource,

00:48:23.010 --> 00:48:25.800
that is a bit of a challenge at the moment

00:48:25.800 --> 00:48:27.720
because of the financial position.

00:48:27.720 --> 00:48:29.371
Julian and I are having
conversations about

00:48:29.371 --> 00:48:32.190
how do we make sure we
are improving finance

00:48:32.190 --> 00:48:34.800
and operations in concert with each other

00:48:34.800 --> 00:48:37.980
and are we appropriately
using all four levels

00:48:37.980 --> 00:48:39.240
of the NOF framework to make sure

00:48:39.240 --> 00:48:40.980
we're directing attention
in the right place.

00:48:40.980 --> 00:48:42.240
And I think there is work to do

00:48:42.240 --> 00:48:44.730
to codify some of the
improvement mechanisms

00:48:44.730 --> 00:48:46.440
to make sure we've got the
right improvement resource

00:48:46.440 --> 00:48:47.273
in the right place

00:48:47.273 --> 00:48:48.750
and make sure improvement resources

00:48:48.750 --> 00:48:49.857
really directed at improvement

00:48:49.857 --> 00:48:51.870
and not just propping things up.

00:48:51.870 --> 00:48:53.130
Is that fair?

00:48:53.130 --> 00:48:53.963
More to do,

00:48:53.963 --> 00:48:57.963
I think is good and more
to do in my opening remark.

